Barry Code128 width-pattern table attribution

The Code128 symbol-width table in src/linear/code128.rs is derived from ZXing's
Code128Reader.CODE_PATTERNS, Copyright 2008 ZXing authors, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. Barry packs the six-width symbol prefixes as integer
constants and handles the stop symbol's seventh width separately. The decoding
implementation is Barry code; no ZXing decoder is used at runtime.

Source: https://github.com/zxing/zxing/blob/zxing-3.5.3/core/src/main/java/com/google/zxing/oned/Code128Reader.java
